<title>GERMANY: Commerzbank launches &quot;electronic purse&quot;.</title>
<headline>Commerzbank launches &quot;electronic purse&quot;.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1996-09-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Commerzbank AG, Germany's second largest commercial bank, on Monday said it was poised to launch a pre-paid electronic chip card -- a relative novelty on the cash-dominated German market.</p>
<p>In a statement the bank said the so-called &quot;electronic purse&quot;, whose inbuilt micro-chip can store a cash value of up to 400 marks, would be tested in a restricted area from October and extended nationwide during 1997.</p>
